post_install() {
    cat << "EOF"

==> MPV Enqueue Configuration

For enqueue to work properly, mpv must read commands from a socket.

Add the following line to your mpv configuration file:

    input-ipc-server=/tmp/mpvsocket

==> open-in-mpv extension installation

This package comes with the Chromium extension, not available on the Chrome Web Store.

To load it in Chromium browsers:
    1. Head to chrome://extensions, or the equivalent of your browser if it doesn't work
    2. Enable "Developer mode"
    3. Click "Load unpacked" and select the directory /usr/lib/open-in-mpv-chromium/

Firefox users:
    The extension is available on the Firefox Add-ons site: https://addons.mozilla.org/pt-PT/firefox/addon/iina-open-in-mpv/

==> Registering the mpv URI handler

To register the mpv URI handler, run:
    xdg-mime default open-in-mpv.desktop x-scheme-handler/mpv

This sets the open-in-mpv desktop file as the default handler for the mpv URI scheme so mpv:// links will open with this package.

EOF
}
